> Ok so if I want to precise each pathway specifically (one pathway poisson, the other normal, etc.), I should use Mplus I guess?

Yes, Mplus has appropriate link functions for count variables, including zero-inflation.  You could also program whatever model you want using a more flexible Bayesian modeling software.  The blavaan package allows you to specify lavaan syntax that will be translated to JAGS syntax, which you can then edit to do things like use a log-linear model for count outcomes.

